Changes made for Atech-crab (2026-11):
  - atech/ (new): firmware for the Atech 14-port board, generated from Sesame's
    firmware/movement-sequences.h; the mg90s_pair servo module; a deck and lid
    replacing Sesame's top cover (from Atech Atelier's "Sesame walker" design);
    print-ready STLs and sliced print files; an assembly guide and video.
  - README.md: an Atech-crab introduction added above Sesame's original README.
  - .gitignore: the Atech SDK's build output.
  - NOTICE (this file): new.
All other files are Sesame's, unchanged.

The Sesame parts in atech/print/stl/ (internal frame, bottom cover, legs) are
Sesame's parts, taken from sesame-ml's model of Sesame
(https://github.com/lukehollis/sesame-ml, Apache-2.0) and turned to their print
orientation.
The internal frame is modified (v6, 2026-11-09): eight lead slots, 9 x 3.4 mm,
cut up from its underside wire channels (Internal-Frame-v121-wired.stl).
Its four deck-screw holes are widened (v6.1, 2026-11-10): head pocket 6.0 mm,
through-hole 2.6 mm.

"Sesame" is the name of Dorian Todd's project. It is used here only to say
where Atech-crab comes from; Atech-crab is not made or endorsed by it.
